{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00723",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.7,
      "end_seconds": 11.21,
      "duration_seconds": 9.51,
      "text": "Hello, doctor! I've brought my son Rohan with me because he keeps me right on dates. I'm Mr Kapoor. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 12.76,
      "end_seconds": 18.22,
      "duration_seconds": 5.46,
      "text": "Hi, doctor. Dad's been constipated since the iron tablets."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.92,
      "end_seconds": 27.01,
      "duration_seconds": 7.09,
      "text": "Pleased to meet you both. Mr Kapoor, when did the constipation start?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.74,
      "end_seconds": 35.54,
      "duration_seconds": 6.8,
      "text": "Oh, a month ago, six weeks, I really can't say, it crept up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 38.02,
      "end_seconds": 43.39,
      "duration_seconds": 5.37,
      "text": "It's been two months, Dad, since they started the iron."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 45.78,
      "end_seconds": 55.18,
      "duration_seconds": 9.4,
      "text": "So between one and two months, we'll say. How often do you go to the toilet now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 58.21,
      "end_seconds": 64.12,
      "duration_seconds": 5.91,
      "text": "Every three or four days. And it's hard. Pellets, like a rabbit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 66.25,
      "end_seconds": 69.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Tell me about your medicines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.32,
      "end_seconds": 84.3,
      "duration_seconds": 11.98,
      "text": "Ferrous sulphate, 200 mg, twice a day, for my anaemia. And metformin, 500 mg, twice a day, for my diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.86,
      "end_seconds": 98.23,
      "duration_seconds": 11.37,
      "text": "That fits. Iron is a very common cause of constipation. Do you have any family history of bowel problems?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 99.95,
      "end_seconds": 106.93,
      "duration_seconds": 6.98,
      "text": "His brother had bowel polyps, doctor. Removed, about ten years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.34,
      "end_seconds": 118.29,
      "duration_seconds": 7.95,
      "text": "Thank you. And what do you eat, any fibre in your diet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.7,
      "end_seconds": 127.69,
      "duration_seconds": 6.99,
      "text": "Rice, dal, a bit of chapatti. Not much fruit. I don't like it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 144.38,
      "end_seconds": 147.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "Let me feel your tummy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.14,
      "end_seconds": 163.56,
      "duration_seconds": 13.42,
      "text": "Your tummy is soft, and I can feel some firm stool in the left lower side. Pulse is 72, blood pressure 130 over 82."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 165.41,
      "end_seconds": 168.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "Is it serious? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.76,
      "end_seconds": 185.39,
      "duration_seconds": 15.63,
      "text": "Not usually, but because you're anaemic, and your brother had polyps, I'd like to look into why you needed the iron in the first place. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.69,
      "end_seconds": 193.53,
      "duration_seconds": 5.84,
      "text": "The iron was for tiredness. They found my blood low. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.72,
      "end_seconds": 208.98,
      "duration_seconds": 13.26,
      "text": "Yes, but not why it was low. I'd like to arrange a blood test, to see how the iron is responding, and I'll check on a bowel referral."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 211.98,
      "end_seconds": 218.22,
      "duration_seconds": 6.24,
      "text": "Can the iron be changed, so he's not blocked up? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.24,
      "end_seconds": 231.77,
      "duration_seconds": 10.53,
      "text": "Yes, we can try one tablet a day, or every other day, which is gentler. Take it with orange juice for absorption."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 234.03,
      "end_seconds": 237.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "Every other day. All right. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.43,
      "end_seconds": 247.16,
      "duration_seconds": 7.73,
      "text": "And a stool softener, plus more fibre, prunes, brown bread, and plenty of water."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 249.86,
      "end_seconds": 254.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.56,
      "text": "Prunes! My wife will be thrilled. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 257.5,
      "end_seconds": 262.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.66,
      "text": "Will a lower dose of iron still work? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.87,
      "end_seconds": 273.0,
      "duration_seconds": 8.13,
      "text": "Yes, it replaces your stores more slowly, but it works, and you'll tolerate it better. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 275.7,
      "end_seconds": 280.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "And how long until I'm not tired? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.5,
      "end_seconds": 292.08,
      "duration_seconds": 8.58,
      "text": "A few weeks, and the blood count will tell us how it's going. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.73,
      "end_seconds": 301.41,
      "duration_seconds": 6.68,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in four weeks, with the blood results."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 303.11,
      "end_seconds": 306.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "We'll be there. ~"
    }
  ]
}
